    {
      "dom_id": "question-68925",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "In Toronto, Canada, the average temperature in November is ${4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ In December, the average temperature decreases by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November. Finally, in January, the average temperature decreases by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the previous month. Determine the average temperature in Toronto in January.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we must determine the average temperature in Toronto during the month of December. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in November. This gives\n\n$$\n{4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature during the month of January. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to December, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Toronto in January is $-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
